// Justification letters (you must use one)
//	l = left
//	c = center

{1000}{37c [This book appears to be someone's journal. The text is mostly day to day musings and personal tidbits, but as you flip through, a few entries catch your eye...]}
{1001}{37l
}
{1002}{37l 09/26/2079 Rhames and Johnson have begun to argue. Johnson acts brave, but I think he's as scared as anybody about why the Transit System suddenly went offline, right when we lost our connection to the Deep Worlds network. We all fear the same thing.
}
{1003}{37l Rhames keeps saying we should venture out, see what's going on in the outside world. I kind of agree- we need to resupply eventually, and with the Transit down, that means going Outside. Johnson is arguing for everyone to stay inside and wait for the network to come back up. I have a frightening feeling the network is *not* coming back up.
}
{1004}{37l 10/22/2079 Well, all communications with the outside world have been down for over three weeks now. We're too deep to get any good radio reception, and no trains have come through the Transit System for over a month. Rhames is threatening to leave the Deep World, and he has some people backing him. Goddamnit, we don't have enough people to divide ourselves up and risk losses! Johnson won't budge though, and I'm worried Rhames is serious.
}
{1005}{37l 12/15/2079 Rhames left. He and twelve others took two of our four guns and disappeared in the middle of the night. We don't know where they went, but we've sealed the Front Gate behind them. They are no longer welcome in this community.}


//TPU Notesfor shutdown sequence puzzle

{1010}{37l These are my collected notes on the proper way to shut down the Trespassing Prevention Unit. It is still in the early stages of development, so please exercise the utmost caution when working with this device. Each Configuration Board needs to be in its own particular configuration for the system to shut down. Each value can only be assigned to one Board.

}
{1011}{37l For shutdown sequence:}
{1012}{37l The Comm Priorities should be in alphabetical order from the first Board to the last. My grecian ancestors would be proud. Make sure Board 3 is not set with Delta or Omega priorities!}
{1013}{37l Board 1's Wave Frequency should be higher than Board 2 but lower than Board 4, and Board 5 needs to be assigned the lowest of all.} 
{1014}{37l Board 5 does not use the IPSI or DLEM Crush Protocols but it seems Board 4 uses the DOOR protocol.}
{1015}{37l Board 1 will definitely not run in Dynamic or Intra Memory Modes, but L5 can't do High or Intra.}
{1016}{37l Board 2's Crush Protocol begins with a consonant. Both Boards 5 and 2's end in consonants. Boards 3 and 5 use Wave Frequencies ending in odd numbers.}
{1017}{37l Board 2's Memory Mode must be able to change easily if necessary.



}
{1018}{37l Reference Appendices:}
{1019}{37l Memory Modes: High, Low, Intra, Dynamic, Assertive.  
Wave Frequencies: 185, 60, 125, 85, 100. 
Crush Protocols: DLEM, ANDY, FLAM, IPSI, DOOR. 
Comm Priorities: Epsilon, Omega, Alpha, Theta, Delta.}



{1020}{[This book is a compendium of information on the inner workings of the Deep15 network.]}
 